------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Libraries in binary distributions
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A jar, war or Docker image also contains the libraries the build resolves
from Maven and npm. Three generated files itemise them and travel with every
binary distribution:

  META-INF/THIRD-PARTY.txt     every Java library in the archive with its
                               version and licence (license-maven-plugin in
                               ujcms-starter/pom.xml; licence names normalised
                               to SPDX identifiers; the build fails on a
                               licence outside the allow-list)
  cp/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt  every npm package bundled into the console,
                               with its licence text (rollup-plugin-license in
                               ujcms-ui-console/vite.config.ts)
  bom.json                     CycloneDX software bill of materials

Licence texts for the families that occur are in licenses/: Apache-2.0, MIT,
BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, EPL-2.0, EDL-1.0, MPL-2.0, LGPL-2.1, CC0-1.0,
the Bouncy Castle licence, the Dameng JDBC Using License, the
Indiana University Extreme! Lab Software License 1.2 and the jsbn licence.
Where a library offers a choice of licences, UJCMS distributes it under the
option named here: Logback, jakarta.annotation, jakarta.json and Parsson
under EPL-2.0; jakarta.mail, Angus Mail and jakarta.activation under EDL-1.0;
JSqlParser and JNA under Apache-2.0. Items with conditions of their own:

  MariaDB Connector/J (LGPL-2.1) is the MySQL / MariaDB driver of every
  edition. It is an unmodified, separate jar (lib/ of the image, BOOT-INF/lib
  of the jar, WEB-INF/lib of the war) and can be replaced by any other build
  of the same library.
  The LibreOffice UNO jars (MPL-2.0) are unmodified; their source is
  available from https://www.libreoffice.org/.
  The Dameng JDBC driver is redistributed under the Dameng JDBC Using License
  reproduced in licenses/Dameng-JDBC.txt.
  mxparser: This product includes software developed by the Indiana
  University Extreme! Lab. For further information please visit
  http://www.extreme.indiana.edu/
  webp-imageio bundles native libwebp (BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2010,
  Google Inc.).

The Docker image is built on bellsoft/liberica-openjre-debian (Liberica JRE,
GPL-2.0 with the Classpath Exception) and installs Debian packages: LibreOffice
(MPL-2.0), the MariaDB command-line client (GPL-2.0; run only as a separate
program by the backup feature), procps, fontconfig and the fonts Noto CJK
(OFL-1.1), Liberation 2 (OFL-1.1), Carlito (OFL-1.1), Caladea (Apache-2.0)
and DejaVu (Bitstream Vera licence). They are aggregated with UJCMS in one
image and stay under their own licences; each package's licence text is in
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the image and their sources are
available from Debian (https://www.debian.org/) and BellSoft
(https://bell-sw.com/). No file of these packages is part of UJCMS.
